8. Follow-up interview question
Interviewer: "Suppose an external payment API processes a payment successfully, but your NestJS application times out before receiving the response. Would you retry the request?"

A strong answer is:

"I wouldn't blindly retry the payment request because the payment might already have been processed. I would use an idempotency key if the payment provider supports it, allowing repeated requests to be identified as the same logical operation. I would also verify the transaction status with the provider when necessary. This helps prevent duplicate payments and maintains consistency between my application and the payment service."